        "original_id": "0f711f8a-9955-5d54-aaf7-692a42cd8ff3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Talaiasi Labalaba\n- Organizations: Royal Ulster Rifles, Royal Irish Rifles, British Army\n- Topics: Infantry regiments, military unit renaming, regimental formation\n\nFacts:\n- In 1881, the Royal Irish Rifles was first created by amalgamating the 83rd (County of Dublin) Regiment of Foot and the 86th (Royal County Down) Regiment of Foot.\n- On 1 January 1921, the Royal Irish Rifles became the Royal Ulster Rifles.\n- The Royal Irish Rifles, later called the Royal Ulster Rifles, was an infantry rifle regiment of the British Army.\n- Talaiasi Labalaba initially served in the British Army in the Royal Ulster Rifles.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
